module bindings.javascript.matrix_device_verification_key_binding;

// A Matrix client SDK finishes an interactive verification (SAS emoji/decimal,
// or a QR scan) by turning the key set the other side MACed into device trust.
// The key set arrives keyed by Matrix key identifiers, `<algorithm>:<id>`, so
// the flow first has to work out what each identifier names: a device the
// client already stores, resolved with `getStoredDevice`, or the user's
// cross-signing identity, resolved with `getStoredCrossSigningForUser`. Both
// lookups are keyed by the same string, and the homeserver is what supplies
// the device list, so nothing about an identifier says which of the two
// namespaces it belongs to.
//
// That is why the trust call matters. `MatrixClient.setDeviceVerified(userId,
// deviceId)` is documented to mark a device verified from the identifier
// alone; `Crypto.setDeviceVerification`'s trailing `keys` argument is
// documented as "the list of keys that was present during the device
// verification", to "be double checked with the list of keys the given device
// has currently". Committing trust with the identifier-only call throws away
// the one thing the verification actually established -- which key the peer
// proved possession of -- so a device whose identifier collides with the
// cross-signing key identifier gets the trust that was earned by the other
// namespace's key.
//
// The binding therefore looks for a single function that resolves both
// namespaces from the offered identifiers and then commits trust by
// identifier, with no key-checking trust call anywhere in it. Each method name
// is matched as a whole `call:` token rather than a substring, so
// `getStoredDevicesForUser` does not stand in for `getStoredDevice` and the
// key-checking `setDeviceVerification` is not read as the identifier-only
// `setDeviceVerified`. A flow that passes the observed keys to
// `setDeviceVerification` satisfies the control and is not reported.
binding matrixDeviceVerificationKeyBindingMissing {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "function" and node.context.language == "javascript" and node.context.call == "getStoredDevice" and node.context.call == "getStoredCrossSigningForUser" and node.context.call == "setDeviceVerified" and not (node.context.call == "setDeviceVerification")
  emit issue code.DeviceVerificationKeyBindingMissing at node
}
